{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not make for yourself a graven image, etc.</b> It is necessary to understand: after He said ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״ etc., even in thought, what need is there further to command concerning the making of graven images? And if the command is about making them even for another's use, if so, He should not have said the word ״לְךָ״. Further, He should not have gone on to say <b>you shall not bow down</b> if the warning came only concerning the craftsman's act. Further, why did He call the images by the name פֶּסֶל? Further, it is necessary to understand why it was necessary to say a second time <b>YHWH your Elohim</b>, for it would have been sufficient to say ״כִּי אָנֹכִי אֵל קַנָּא,״ and the matter returns to the Speaker at the beginning: ״אָנֹכִי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ.״ Further, it is necessary to understand why it was necessary to give a reason <b>for</b> etc. <b>El qa-na</b> (a jealous El) — for even without this reason, are they not obligated to accept the decree of the King of the world, blessed is He?" "<b>And it appears</b> that He intends to state a prohibition of a category of idolatry other than that mentioned in the verse ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ,״ and it is as follows. A person may say: the truth is that YHWH is the Elohim and all besides Him is nothing, but given the immensity of His greatness, a human being's capacity and comprehension are diminished to speak before Him and to ask the details of his requests, for it is not consistent with the protocol of honor that a lowly, dark creature like myself should come and ask questions before the great and awesome King — and sometimes one has many details of one's needs, both minor and numerous, and how could one have such brazenness to multiply inquiries before Him. Therefore he will take counsel with his inclination to choose to speak his words before one of the ministers who serve before Him on high, and that one will help him and also serve as an intermediary to speak his words before the great King in a great matter if necessary; and through such mediation he will greatly honor that minister and bless him and bow down before him with all honor and exaltation, for by this he hopes to win his favor to bear his burden and attend to his needs. And know that in this error erred most of those who worship idolatry, for they know that they are not worshipping a god but only so that it may serve them as an intermediary, etc., as mentioned. And this category is not called by the name 'god' but rather פֶּסֶל, for he knows that it is not a god, and this is its פְּסִלוּת (invalidity/uselessness) — that it possesses no divine power, and it is פְּסֹלֶת (dross/refuse) before the Primary, who is the Creator of the world. Or He called it <b>פֶּסֶל</b> because it stands to be nullified (לְהִתְפַּסֵּל) when YHWH removes it from its dominion, whether through some cause or through the very act of the one who bows to it which causes its nullification — in the manner our Sages of blessed memory said (Eichah Rabbah, ch. 2) regarding the generation of the Flood, who said: ״We adjure the ministering angels appointed over us,״ etc., and YHWH removed the dominion of the angels, as it says (Isaiah 43:28) ״וַאֲחַלֵּל שָׂרֵי קֹדֶשׁ.״ And YHWH commanded also concerning this category and said <b>you shall not make for yourself a פֶּסֶל</b> — meaning, even though you yourself know in your mind that it is a פֶּסֶל, nevertheless you shall not make it for yourself." "And He returned and explained what the act is, and said <b>you shall not bow down to them</b> etc. And He stated the reason for the prohibition: <b>for I YHWH your El am jealous</b> — meaning, I am jealous over the matter even if it be in this manner. To understand the content of this intention, behold, we find that YHWH mentioned this particular detail of jealousy in the portion of Naso (Numbers 5:14), as it is written ״וְעָבַר עָלָיו רוּחַ קִנְאָה וְקִנֵּא אֶת אִשְׁתּוֹ״ etc. Now, sometimes a man is jealous of his wife on account of his son or his servant. And you already know that Israel are in the aspect of a bride, as is hinted at length in the holy of holies book, Song of Songs. And from this, when Israel make for themselves masters — even though they do not rebel and do not deny the Creator, for He is Lord of lords — reason demands that the Husband become jealous. And the parable for this: a king's wife who loves a servant of the king or his son, to attend to the details she needs from them, and she embraces him and kisses him — would the king not be jealous enough to stab her with a sword? So too is this matter. And one who discerns the manner of the soul's attachment with Israel and the Creator, with desire, with longing, with attachment in great love, will attain the contemplation of the one who understands. And this is what He said: <b>for I YHWH your Elohim</b> — He was precise to say ״your Elohim״ to allude to what was said, and it is the sod of the indwelling of His Shekhinah, blessed is He, upon Israel and the unification of His name, and the discerning one will understand. And therefore you will find that the verse says (Deuteronomy 4:19) ״אֲשֶׁר חָלַק ה׳״ etc., to all the peoples — for the peoples have their princes, the celestial princes, and they are those who rule over them; not so the children of Israel — He is our King, He is our Prince, He is our Elohim, blessed is He." "<b>And by way of</b> remez (allusion), He alludes in saying <b>you shall not make for yourself a פֶּסֶל</b> — meaning, that one should not invalidate (יִפְסוֹל) oneself, for when a person sins with the sin of idolatry, which stands against the entire Torah in its entirety, by his very nature he becomes נִפְסָל (invalidated/disqualified) and the divine image is removed, as it is written (Psalms 39:7) ״אַךְ בְּצֶלֶם יִתְהַלֶּךְ אִישׁ,״ and his face is not seen on high, and he enters the category of prohibition for the children of the living El, that they may not gaze upon his face, as the prophet said to the king of Israel (II Kings 3:14) ״לוּלֵי פְּנֵי יְהוֹשָׁפָט״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :register {:flags {2 ["Lord"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:56.564931959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}